Subject: [PATCH] arm64: fix the icache line size shift in arch_cpu_sync_icache

arch_cpu_sync_icache() reads CTR_EL0 and is supposed to pull IminLine out
of bits [3:0] with `ctr_el0 & 0xF` -- the same way it correctly pulls
DminLine out of bits [19:16] two lines below with `(ctr_el0 >> 16) & 0xF`,
and the same way compiler-rt's __clear_cache (which this function's
commit message says it was derived from) computes it. Instead it does
`ctr_el0 << 0xF`, shifting CTR_EL0 itself left by 15 instead of masking
its low 4 bits.

`4 << (ctr_el0 << 0xF)` shifts `int` by a change-of-register amount that
is well past the width of the type, which is undefined behavior in C++
and compiles to whatever the `lsl` instruction happens to do with a huge
shift-amount register -- not a fixed wrong constant, so the resulting
icache_line_size can come out as 0. When it does, the invalidation loop

    for (uint64_t address_icache = ROUNDDOWN(addr, icache_line_size);
         address_icache < end; address_icache += icache_line_size) {

never advances and spins forever at 100% CPU, which is exactly what
every path that calls arch_cpu_sync_icache() after writing executable
pages (module/driver loading, runtime_loader, the kernel debugger's
breakpoint patching) runs into. Confirmed by sampling the stuck vCPU's
PC in a tight loop under QEMU/hvf -- it kept landing inside this
function, specifically in the icache invalidation loop -- right after
the exact point in boot where a kernel module gets loaded (observed
with the ethernet drivers, but any module load hits the same path).
Whether a given run hangs depends on the exact bit pattern QEMU's
emulated CTR_EL0 produces for this build, which is also why this has
been intermittent rather than a guaranteed hang on every boot.

This is upstream Haiku arm64 code (src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/arch_cpu.cpp,
introduced in 6bcb56f62dfd20138ddc4194972f6eec7101800d, "arm64: Implement
icache synchronization to match documentation"), not something this
port's own patches touch -- it affects any arm64 Haiku boot where
CTR_EL0's IminLine field happens to produce a shift-amount-mod-bit-width
of 0 after being left-shifted by 15, not just this port's QEMU test
environment. Worth upstreaming once confirmed fixed here.

diff --git a/src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/arch_cpu.cpp b/src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/arch_cpu.cpp
index b1ac3478a6..a3a932d1b0 100644
--- a/src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/arch_cpu.cpp
+++ b/src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/arch_cpu.cpp
@@ -104,7 +104,7 @@ arch_cpu_sync_icache(void *address, size_t len)
 	uint64_t ctr_el0 = 0;
 	asm volatile ("mrs\t%0, ctr_el0":"=r" (ctr_el0));

-	uint64_t icache_line_size = 4 << (ctr_el0 << 0xF);
+	uint64_t icache_line_size = 4 << (ctr_el0 & 0xF);
 	uint64_t dcache_line_size = 4 << ((ctr_el0 >> 16) & 0xF);
 	uint64_t addr = (uint64_t)address;
 	uint64_t end = addr + len;
